  "notes": [
    "Partial encoding from Alaska Medicaid Viberzi Criteria Version 1. Viberzi (eluxadoline), a mu-opioid receptor agonist, is indicated for adults with IBS-D; tablets 75 mg and 100 mg.",
    "Source dates: Original 8/06/2018; Approval 9/21/2018. effective_date 2018-01-01 is an extracted metadata stub, not either actual PDF date.",
    "Approval predicates encode adult IBS-D, no concomitant opioids or benzodiazepine, and the three required medication trials. The failed_* fact names represent trial completion; the source does not explicitly require documented failure.",
    "Denial predicates encode known hypersensitivity/contraindication/intolerance attestation and all six concrete clinical exclusions. A negative response confirms absence; missing safety responses require more information.",
    "Cautions (notes only): monitor for pancreatitis and sphincter of Oddi spasm, including new or worsening abdominal pain with or without nausea/vomiting, or acute biliary pain with liver or pancreatic enzyme elevations; immediately discontinue Viberzi and seek medical attention if symptoms develop.",
    "Cautions (notes only): stop Viberzi and immediately contact the healthcare provider for severe constipation; avoid other drugs that may cause constipation (e.g. opioids).",
    "Authorization (notes only): initial approval up to 3 months; reauthorization up to 12 months with a reported improvement.",
    "Quantity limits (notes only): 60 tablets of 75 mg per month; 60 tablets of 100 mg per month."
  ],
